    "statement": "A gross-Sharpe floor measured in the planted worlds OVERSTATES what a real book needs to clear key 2. The planted books are much less volatile than read 3's, so the same cost in basis points costs them far more Sharpe: their median monthly volatility is about 0.57 to 0.62 per cent against read 3's 1.24 per cent, and they lose a median 0.79 to 0.85 of annualised Sharpe to costs against read 3's 0.42. Key 2 is a bar on a real book's NET Sharpe, so it must be read in net units, not inferred from a gross floor.",
